          explanation: 'Only the homozygous recessive genotype (aa, with a probability of 1/4 or 25%) shows the albino phenotype; all other possible genotypes (AA and Aa) result in a normal (unaffected) appearance, which is why the phenotypically unaffected probability (75%) is higher than the probability of any single non-affected genotype alone.',
