          explanation: 'This gradual, directional sequence of anatomical change across a well-ordered series of fossils is interpreted as strong evidence of evolutionary change over time within the horse lineage, likely reflecting a shift in habitat and diet from browsing in forested environments to grazing on more open grassland, with natural selection favouring traits (larger size, fewer toes for running, grazing-adapted teeth) suited to this changing environment.',
