          explanation: 'Because sons receive their only X chromosome from their mother, a son has a 50% chance of inheriting the mother’s Xh allele (and being affected, since he has no second X to mask it with XH); daughters, however, always receive an XH from their unaffected father, which is dominant over any Xh they may inherit from their mother, so no daughter from this cross can be affected.',
