          explanation: 'This effect is described as "unreliable" because it depends on maintaining a specific, frequent breastfeeding pattern; as feeding frequency naturally decreases over time (or if it is interrupted), prolactin levels fall, and ovulation — often without any obvious preceding signs, such as a period — can resume unpredictably, sometimes before the mother realises fertility has returned.',
