          answer: 'Negative feedback is a homeostatic control mechanism in which a deviation from a set point triggers a response that counteracts (reduces) that deviation, returning the variable back toward its normal set point.',
          explanation: 'Negative feedback is the dominant mechanism used throughout the body to maintain stable internal conditions, since it actively works to reduce (rather than amplify) any deviation from normal.',
