          prompt: 'Define egestion, and explain how it differs from excretion.',
          answer: 'Egestion is the removal of undigested food (faeces) from the body via the anus; it differs from excretion in that egested material was never actually absorbed into the body’s cells, whereas excreted substances are true metabolic waste products that were produced inside the body.',
          explanation: 'This distinction matters because faeces contain substances (such as indigestible fibre and dead gut bacteria) that were never part of the body’s internal chemistry, unlike genuine metabolic wastes such as urea.',
