          prompt: 'Name the enzyme secreted by the stomach that begins the chemical digestion of protein, and state the pH conditions under which it works best.',
          answer: 'Pepsin; it works best in strongly acidic conditions (a low pH, provided by hydrochloric acid in the stomach).',
          explanation: 'This is why the stomach’s hydrochloric acid does not merely kill ingested bacteria — it also creates the specific acidic environment pepsin needs to be active, since pepsin would be far less effective at the near-neutral pH found elsewhere in the digestive tract.',
