          answer: 'Urea is removed mainly by the kidneys (in urine); carbon dioxide is removed mainly by the lungs (during exhalation).',
          explanation: 'Because different metabolic wastes are produced by different processes in the body (urea from the breakdown of excess amino acids in the liver; carbon dioxide from cellular respiration), different organs have become specialised to remove each one efficiently.',
