          explanation: 'This shows why carrying capacity is not merely an abstract ecological concept but a practically essential figure for real-world conservation and wildlife management decisions, where both overestimating and underestimating it can lead to poor management outcomes — either unnecessary population control or damaging habitat overuse.',
