          explanation: 'This distinguishes a problem of oxygen transport (as in anaemia, where haemoglobin itself is deficient) from a problem of gaseous exchange (as in a lung disease affecting the alveoli directly) — the two are separate stages of getting oxygen to the body’s cells, and either can be impaired independently of the other.',
