          answer: 'An ecosystem is a community of interacting living organisms together with the non-living (abiotic) components of their environment (such as soil, water, air and climate), all interacting as a functional unit.',
          explanation: 'An ecosystem includes both the biotic community (all interacting populations of different species) and the abiotic environment those organisms interact with, distinguishing it from a community, which refers only to the living organisms themselves.',
