          difficulty: 'Moderate',
          marks: 4,
          prompt: 'Describe the structure and function of phloem tissue.',
          answer: 'Phloem tissue is composed of living sieve tube elements, joined end to end with perforated end walls (sieve plates), together with adjacent companion cells that support them. Phloem transports (translocates) dissolved organic nutrients, mainly sucrose, from the parts of the plant producing or storing them to the parts of the plant using or storing them.',
