          explanation: 'Together, these three features ensure the leaf can both capture the maximum amount of light energy and maintain an efficient supply of carbon dioxide to (and removal of oxygen from) its photosynthesising cells, which is why a leaf is often described as being structurally optimised for photosynthesis.',
