          answer: 'A population is all the individuals of the same species living in a particular area at the same time, for example, all the impala in a game reserve. A community is all the different populations of different species living and interacting together in the same area, for example, all the impala, lions, grass and trees together within a game reserve.',
          explanation: 'A community therefore always consists of more than one population, since it includes every interacting species population sharing that same area, not just a single species.',
