          explanation: 'Each of these structural differences reflects the fundamentally different way plant and animal cells obtain energy and maintain their shape — plant cells rely on photosynthesis and a rigid, turgid structure for support, while animal cells rely on consuming food and, in multicellular animals, an internal skeleton and active movement for support.',
