          answer: 'The atmosphere (as carbon dioxide gas) and fossil fuels (coal, oil and natural gas) — (the oceans and limestone rock are also acceptable).',
          explanation: 'Carbon continuously moves between these physical reservoirs and living organisms as it cycles through the ecosystem, entering organisms mainly through photosynthesis and leaving mainly through respiration, combustion and decomposition.',
