          prompt: 'Describe the structure and function of collenchyma tissue, referring to its cell walls.',
          answer: 'Collenchyma consists of living cells with unevenly thickened cell walls (thickened mainly at the corners), made of cellulose and pectin, without lignin. It provides flexible mechanical support to the still-growing parts of a plant, such as young stems and leaf stalks, allowing them to bend without breaking.',
