          answer: 'Simple columnar epithelium is composed of a single layer of tall, column-shaped cells. It is well suited to secretion and absorption, since its tall cells have room to contain the numerous organelles, such as many mitochondria and extensive endoplasmic reticulum, needed to actively produce secretions or absorb substances — for example, lining the inside of the small intestine, where it absorbs digested nutrients.',
