          marks: 6,
          context: 'Two transverse sections of a dicotyledonous plant are examined. In section A the vascular tissue lies in separate bundles arranged in a ring near the outside, with xylem towards the inside of each bundle and phloem towards the outside. In section B the vascular tissue lies as a single star-shaped core in the centre, with strips of phloem between the arms of the xylem.',
          prompt: 'Identify the organ shown in section A and in section B, give a reason for each identification, and explain ONE advantage of the arrangement seen in each organ.',
