          marks: 4,
          prompt: 'Describe the function of the dendrites, the axon and the myelin sheath of a motor neuron, and name the cells that support and protect neurons.',
          answer: 'The dendrites receive impulses from other neurons and carry them towards the cell body. The axon carries the impulse away from the cell body to the effector, which in this case is a muscle. The myelin sheath insulates the axon and speeds up conduction by making the impulse jump between the gaps in the sheath, and it also protects the axon. Neurons are supported and protected by neuroglia, also called glial cells.',
