          prompt: 'Identify the producer and the top carnivore in this web, and give TWO reasons why a food web represents feeding relationships more realistically than a single food chain.',
          answer: 'The producer is the grass and the top carnivore is the owl. A food web is more realistic because most animals eat more than one type of food and are themselves eaten by more than one predator, as the guineafowl here eats both grasshoppers and mice, which a single chain cannot show; and because a web shows the interconnections between chains, so it can be used to predict how a change in the number of one species will affect several others rather than only the species directly above and below it.',
