          answer: 'The pyramid is inverted at the base because a pyramid of numbers counts individual organisms without considering their size, and a single very large marula tree can supply food for thousands of small caterpillars, so the producer bar represents one organism while the primary consumer bar represents many. The ecologist could redraw the data as a pyramid of biomass, in which the dry mass of the organisms at each level is plotted instead of their number, because the mass of the one large tree is far greater than the total mass of the caterpillars feeding on it, so the diagram takes on the normal upright pyramid shape; a pyramid of energy would show the same upright shape for the same reason.',
