          grade: 10,
          difficulty: 'Easy',
          marks: 3,
          prompt: 'Name the process in the nitrogen cycle responsible for each of the following: (a) the conversion of ammonia to nitrites and then to nitrates in the soil; (b) the conversion of nitrates in the soil to nitrogen gas; (c) the conversion of atmospheric nitrogen into ammonia inside the root nodules of a bean plant.',
          answer: '(a) Nitrification; (b) denitrification; (c) nitrogen fixation.',
          explanation: 'Each step is carried out by a different group of soil bacteria, namely nitrifying bacteria, denitrifying bacteria and nitrogen-fixing bacteria such as Rhizobium in the root nodules.',
