          context: 'The relative numbers of three organelles were estimated in three cells. Cell X: chloroplasts many, mitochondria moderate, ribosomes moderate. Cell Y: chloroplasts none, mitochondria very many, ribosomes moderate. Cell Z: chloroplasts none, mitochondria moderate, ribosomes very many.',
          prompt: 'Match cell X, cell Y and cell Z to a palisade mesophyll cell, a human sperm cell and a cell of the pancreas that secretes enzymes, and justify each choice.',
          answer: 'Cell X is the palisade mesophyll cell, because only a plant cell exposed to light contains many chloroplasts, and photosynthesis is its main activity. Cell Y is the human sperm cell, because it has no chloroplasts and contains very many mitochondria packed into the middle piece to release the large amount of ATP needed for the tail to beat continuously as the cell swims. Cell Z is the enzyme-secreting pancreas cell, because it has no chloroplasts and contains very many ribosomes, which are the sites where amino acids are joined to build the large quantities of digestive enzyme protein that the cell exports.',
          explanation: 'The abundance of an organelle is a direct clue to the dominant activity of a cell, so matching cells to organelle counts is really matching structure to function.',
