          answer: 'A tissue is a group of cells with a common origin that are structurally similar or work together and that are specialised to carry out one particular function. Parenchyma is a simple tissue because it is made up of only one kind of cell, namely thin-walled living parenchyma cells, all of much the same structure. Xylem is a complex tissue because it is made up of several different kinds of cell working together as one unit, namely vessels and tracheids that conduct water, xylem fibres that give support and xylem parenchyma that stores food, some of which are dead at maturity and some of which are alive.',
          explanation: 'The simple and complex classification is based on the number of cell types in the tissue and not on how complicated the function is, which is why a conducting tissue with several cell types is complex.',
